cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "agent-security-measurement: a source-verified database of publicly disclosed AI agent security incidents"
abstract: >-
  A source-verified database of 245 publicly disclosed candidate security incidents involving AI agents
  (January 2024 - September 2026), with event, campaign and root-cause identifiers, inclusion tiers,
  mechanism, operating-environment and trust-boundary classifications, and links to 1,096 evidence claims.
  A minimal analysis script reproduces the principal population-definition and trust-boundary results of
  Standard AI Technical Note 03, an example of research using the database.
  The data are a curated collection of public disclosures, not a representative sample of deployed AI systems.
authors:
  - family-names: Woollard
    given-names: "David M."
repository-code: "https://github.com/woollard/agent-security-measurement"
url: "https://github.com/woollard/agent-security-measurement"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - AI security
  - incident data
  - measurement
  - trust boundaries
references:
  - type: report
    title: "What Counts as an Agent Security Failure? Population Definitions and Trust Boundaries in Reported AI Agent Incidents"
    authors:
      - family-names: Woollard
        given-names: "David M."
    institution:
      name: "Standard AI"
    year: 2026
    month: 10
    url: "https://labs.standard.ai/notes/Note-03.pdf"
    notes: "Standard AI Technical Note 03."
